MCP ServerNew · Claude SkillsProduction SEO Skills for Claude Seven ready-to-use Claude Skills wrap the SE Ranking MCP into finished SEO deliverables: AI Search share of voice, backlink gap, content briefs, keyword clusters, paid-search intelligence, content audits, and SERP-fit (SXO) analysis.Open source · MIT license · Drops into Claude Code, Claude Desktop, or any MCP clientThe Model Context Protocol (MCP) server provides a standardized interface that allows any compatible AI model or agent to access your SE Ranking data in a simple and secure way.Connect to our MCP server natively in Claude, Cursor, and other clients or use the mcp-remote module for backwards compatibility with clients that do not support remote MCP.SE Ranking’s MCP server follows the authenticated remote MCP spec, so the server is centrally hosted and managed. The SE Ranking MCP server has 160+ tools available for keyword research, backlink analysis, domain analysis, website audits, AI search visibility, SERP analysis, and project management, with more functionality on the way, and feedback on its functionality is welcomed.Setup InstructionsGeneralOur MCP server supports Streamable HTTP transports. This transport uses OAuth 2.1 with dynamic client registration for authentication at the following address:https://api.seranking.com/mcpFor instructions for specific clients, read on.Sub-accountsIf you’re a sub-account on a shared SE Ranking workspace, the Sign in with SE Ranking button won’t connect any tools. API access lives with the master account, not with sub-accounts. Sub-account API keys are on the way; until they’re released, use the workaround below.To connect a sub-account:Get the API key from your account administrator. It’s in the API Dashboard.In the connection dialog, choose Enter API key manually instead of Sign in with SE Ranking.Paste the key when prompted.ClaudeClaude.ai (Web)Navigate to the connectors page, click + and select Add custom connectorSet Name to SE RankingSet Remote MCP server URL to https://api.seranking.com/mcpClick Add. SE Ranking will appear under Not connected.Select SE Ranking and click Connect to authorize.Claude DesktopOpen Claude Desktop and go to Customize > ConnectorsClick + and select Add custom connectorSet Name to SE RankingSet Remote MCP server URL to https://api.seranking.com/mcpClick Add. SE Ranking will appear under Not connected.Select SE Ranking and click Connect to authorize.Claude CodeTwo options. Pick one.Option A: OAuth (recommended) — opens a browser on first connect, stores the token locally, and reuses it across sessions.claude mcp add --transport http se-ranking https://api.seranking.com/mcpThen run /mcp once you’ve opened a Claude Code session to go through the authentication flow.Option B: API key — skip the OAuth flow and pass your key as headers. Right for headless environments, CI runners, shared dev boxes, or when the browser handoff is awkward.claude mcp add --transport http se-ranking https://api.seranking.com/mcp \
  --header "X-Api-Key: *****"Grab the key from the API Dashboard. The API key powers Data/Research tools (keywords, backlinks, domain overview, SERP, AI Search) and Project Management tools (rank tracker, audits, competitors, prompt monitoring).CodexThe setup steps for the MCP server are the same regardless of whether you use the IDE Extension or the CLI since the configuration is shared.Configuration via CLI:Run the following command in Terminal:codex mcp add se-ranking --url https://api.seranking.com/mcpThis will automatically prompt you to log in with your SE Ranking account and connect it to your Codex.Note: If this is the first time you are using an MCP in Codex you will need to enable the rmcp feature for this to work. Add the following into your ~/.codex/config.toml:[features]
experimental_use_rmcp_client = trueConfiguration through environment variables:1. Open the ~/.codex/config.toml file in your preferred editor.2. Add the following:[features]
experimental_use_rmcp_client = true
[mcp_servers.se-ranking]
url = "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"3. Run codex mcp login se-ranking to move through the authentication flow.CursorAdd the following to .cursor/mcp.json (project) or ~/.cursor/mcp.json (global):{
  "mcpServers": {
    "se-ranking": {
      "url": "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"
    }
  }
}Cursor supports Streamable HTTP and OAuth natively. An OAuth window will open on first use to authenticate with your SE Ranking account.Visual Studio Code{
  "mcpServers": {
    "se-ranking": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"]
    }
  }
}1. Ctrl+P / Cmd+P and search for MCP: Add Server.2. Select Command (stdio).3. Enter the following configuration, and hit enter:npx -y mcp-remote https://api.seranking.com/mcp4. Enter the name SE Ranking and hit enter.5. Activate the server using MCP: List Servers, selecting se-ranking, and selecting Start Server.v0 by VercelTo add the MCP to v0, you can install from the connections page.Windsurf1. Ctrl+, / Cmd+, to open Windsurf settings.2. Scroll to Cascade > MCP servers.3. Select Add Server > Add custom server.4. Add the following:{
  "mcpServers": {
    "se-ranking": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"]
    }
  }
}ZedCmd+, to open Zed settings. Add the following:{
  "context_servers": {
    "se-ranking": {
      "source": "custom",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"],
      "env": {}
    }
  }
}Gemini CLIAdd to ~/.gemini/settings.json:{
  "mcpServers": {
    "se-ranking": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"]
    }
  }
}Save and launch Gemini CLI. Authorize when prompted.OthersHundreds of other tools now support MCP servers. You can configure them to use SE Ranking’s MCP server with the following settings:Command: npxArguments: -y mcp-remote https://api.seranking.com/mcpEnvironment: NoneFAQ Why am I seeing an internal server error when trying to connect?Enter the following in the Terminal to clear saved auth info: rm -rf ~/.mcp-auth then try again to connect.Additionally you may need to update to a newer version of Node if required.  What happens when I connect?A browser window opens to seranking.com where you log in with your SE Ranking account and approve access. After approval, you’re redirected back to your client and the connection is established. If the window doesn’t open automatically, check your client for a URL to paste into a browser manually. How do I know the connection worked?Claude.ai / Desktop: SE Ranking moves out of Not connected and its tools become available in chats.Claude Code: Run /mcp and confirm se-ranking shows as connected with 160+ tools.Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, Zed: The server appears as connected in the MCP panel and tools are listed.All clients: Try a prompt like “Using SE Ranking MCP, give me traffic for seranking.com in the US.” If it returns real data, it works.   I’m using WSL on Windows, and seeing an errorWSL can have issues with the OAuth redirect. Configure the server in your client’s Windows-side config file instead, or run the setup from PowerShell:{
  "mcpServers": {
    "se-ranking": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://api.seranking.com/mcp"]
    }
  }
}  Does the MCP support Streamable HTTP?Yes, at the https://api.seranking.com/mcp endpoint.  Can I authenticate with my own API key or OAuth access tokens?The MCP server supports passing OAuth tokens and API key directly in the Authorization: Bearer <your-token> header instead of using the interactive authentication flow.You can use this to interact with the MCP server programmatically, provide read-only access through a restricted API key, or integrate with an existing SE Ranking OAuth application without an extra authentication hop.  No tools appearing after connecting?Verify your SE Ranking account has API access at the API Dashboard.Run /mcp in Claude Code to check live connection status.Try removing and re-adding the server. If you need further assistance, contact us at [email protected].ResourcesVideo: SE Ranking MCP in ActionSee the MCP server in action. Two ways in: a quick 2-minute demo, or go deep with a full workshop run by the team that builds the API.Full live workshops, run by the team that builds the API      From data to action: building automated SEO workflows with MCP & GA4The remote MCP launch, live: connect SE Ranking to Claude in two clicks with OAuth (no Docker, no terminal), layer in GA4, and run an AI search visibility audit across ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, and Google AI Overviews. Closes with a live audience Q&A.Presented by Guifré Ballester (Senior PM, API) & Oleksii Khoroshun (SEO team), SE RankingMay 12, 2026 · 56 min      Claude Code for SEO: building a data-backed marketing agent with SE Ranking MCPA full Claude Code build, live: set an objective, let the agent break it into steps, and pull live competitor, keyword, and AI search signals into a prioritized content plan and publish-ready briefs. Covers repeatable workflows with CLAUDE.md, skills, subagents, and hooks.Presented by Guifré Ballester (Senior PM, API) & Anastasia Kotsiubynska (SEO Team Lead), SE RankingFeb 24, 2026 · 1 h 10 min      Connect your AI to live SEO data: real-time keyword and competitor research with MCPThe original MCP server walkthrough, live: connect SE Ranking’s Data API to Claude and Gemini, then run keyword research, competitor analysis, backlink checks, and AI visibility queries in chat. Real prompts and audience Q&A.Presented by Guifré Ballester (Senior PM, API), SE RankingNov 18, 2025 · 1 h 5 minGo deeper into a specific task      Turn Claude into a full SEO assistant with SE Ranking MCPZoom into a single task: ask Claude an SEO question in plain English and watch the back-and-forth pull live SE Ranking data, here a competitor analysis (Visa vs Mastercard) that surfaces lost keywords and content gaps. No spreadsheets.SE Ranking · 1 min 47 sec
